Accordingly, I respectfully urge the Commission to: 
• Reject any proposal to terminate, sunset, or geographically restrict the E-Rate program; 
• Reject restrictions on consultant compensation structures except in cases of demonstrated waste, 
fraud, or abuse; 
• Reject any proposal to impose federal screen time or instructional technology use limits on 
schools and libraries; 
• Extend the comment period to at least 90 days following Federal Register publication; 
• Ensure that any new administrative requirements are scalable and do not create undue burden on 
applicants of varying size, staffing, or resource levels.
